# The wallpaper, owned by dinit for the same reason yambar is: an
# autostart entry's lifetime belongs to nobody, and the pkill that cleaned
# up the previous session's copy raced its teardown. See yambar for the
# full account, including the stop/start asymmetry -- everything there
# applies here unchanged.
#
# THE FILE-OR-COLOUR CHOICE LIVES IN scripts/swaybg-start, AND THE MOVE WAS
# PAID FOR: the first version inlined it here as `sh -c '...'`, and dinit's
# parser honours double quotes only -- the single quotes passed through as
# literal characters, the shell died on an unterminated quoted string, and
# the service crash-looped with exit code 2 until the restart limit stopped
# it (run 86565312453). Anything worth quoting goes in a script; a command
# line here stays plain tokens.
type = process
command = /bin/busybox sh /etc/dinit.d/scripts/swaybg-start
run-as = veron
restart = true
depends-on = labwc
depends-on = xdg-runtime
depends-on = device-nodes
